<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arras</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Nemetocenna</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arras is a city in the Pas-de-Calais <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and the historic capital of Artois. It began as Nemetocenna, the chief town of the Gallic Atrebates, whose name survives in Arras and Artois. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it grew rich on wool and tapestry weaving, so that 'arras' became an English word for tapestry, and it gave its name to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/union-of-arras">Union of Arras</a> of 1579.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arras.jpg" alt="Arras" width="320" height="194" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: JackyM59 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Le_palais_des_Etats_d%27Artois_et_le_Beffroi_-_Arras.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
